{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"851195444457242675","content":"With his hat of thought still on his head, Roy says:\n\"Manhattan.\"\n\"Within Love and hope,\nthe bond of family is found\nthat no darkness can divide\"\n\n\"Ferrytown.\"\n\"Just as order can be found in chaos, \nthe strength of a community comes from its diverse people.\nA society is the amalgamation of minds, values, hopes, and histories,\nso that no matter what price is asked, the community becomes stronger than iron.\"\n\n\"Staaten Island.\"\n\"Just as hope is the light that guides man safely through troubled waters\nThe spirit of man weathers any storm, \nGiving them the resolve needed to build a better tomorrow.\"\n\n\"Kingsbridge.\"\n\"Thoughts and memories are both food and poison.\nThe difference between whether they sustain or defeat you is in Veracity and Self Discipline. \"Is it true?\" and \"can I endure the truth of it? \"\nThoughts can be intelligence or base cunning. Memories can be wisdom or a prison. \nLet Veracity lead to Wisdom and Wisdom back to truth.\nLet us not be divided on the surety of either.\nLet your thoughts and memories cause others to rise as you rise.\"\n\n\"Hampstead.\"\n\nAfter that, he starts slowly tracing the inscription on the stone, speaking the inscription out loud as he writes.\n\n```Fear of loss drives all strife.\n\nTruth is the only path to liberty.\n\nLet Justice and Mercy be equal.```\n\nRoy finishes the inscription. (now just speaking, not saying as he writes)\n\n\"Empire City. We stand here to mend you together, through hardships and sacrifices. Let us sculpt you into a place for everyone's freedom. In return, let us become and stay the right, good people to maintain you. Let us never give up.\"","created_at":"2021-08-21T09:45:54.234000Z","edited_at":"2021-08-21T09:47:29.742000Z","id":"878575633758846976","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"851195444457242675","content":"As Roy traces the words on the stone, runes and glyphs that were already on the stone show up as if they had always been there. A white line connects the Mender to the original cornerstone of Empire city.  The ground around Roy trembles, as the runes spread out.  Every Cornerstone in Empire city briefly sends runes towards the others, and for one brief moment, there is a web of Arcane energy connecting the hearts of each borough.  The Mender howls in pain, slowly becoming more insubstantial.  His body becomes more like a humanoid made of plants and water as he fades, and as Roy finishes the last word, the Mender briefly vanishes.  When he reappears, he looks tired.  He looks drained.\n\n <@!313689699627696139> The Hampstead cornerstone is repaired.  <@!403783497564684291> <@!148682928434577408> <@!150319814836092928> <@!443806147649208341> <@!339235123759153162> , you all have a sense that the Mending is done.  You were successful.\n\nGil breaths hard \"Mender......\" he reaches to his head \"you are the Mender now....\" He collapses.  He is alive, but unconscious.  Roy is now attuned to the Scriber\n\nGils story in EC is not done... but he is no longer 'the mender'","created_at":"2021-08-21T09:54:12.669000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"878577724346748948","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
